  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Leading**: The player with the heaviest tile (8-7 being the heaviest in this set) leads first. 2. **Matching**: On your turn, you must place a tile where one of its ends matches an available end on the board. 3. **The Draw**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you find a playable tile. (Common house rule: maximum of 3 draws). 4. **Passing**: If the boneyard is empty and you cannot play, you pass. 5. **Ending**: A round ends when one player 'Dominoes' (empties their hand) or when the game is blocked.",
    Player: "1. **Leading**: The player with the heaviest tile (8-7 being the heaviest in this set) leads first. 2. **Matching**: On your turn, you must place a tile where one of its ends matches an available end on the board. 3. **The Draw**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you find a playable tile. (Common house rule: maximum of 3 draws). 4. **Passing**: If the boneyard is empty and you cannot play, you pass. 5. **Ending**: A round ends when one player 'Dominoes' (empties their hand) or when the game is blocked.",
    objective: 'To be the first player to reach 100 points across multiple rounds.',
    gameplay: "1. **Leading**: The player with the heaviest tile (8-7 being the heaviest in this set) leads first. 2. **Matching**: On your turn, you must place a tile where one of its ends matches an available end on the board. 3. **The Draw**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you find a playable tile. (Common house rule: maximum of 3 draws). 4. **Passing**: If the boneyard is empty and you cannot play, you pass. 5. **Ending**: A round ends when one player 'Dominoes' (empties their hand) or when the game is blocked.",
    keyRules: [
      'No Doubles: The absence of doubles means every tile is distinct and has two different numbers.',
      'The 8-7 Lead: The highest tile in play (8-7) always starts the first hand.',
      'Brick Formation: The tableau grows in two directions from the starting tile, but specifically in a side-by-side matching manner.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2-3 players (Draw game) or 4 players (Block game).',
      deck: '36 tiles. To prepare, take a Double-Eight set (45 tiles) and discard all 9 doubles (0-0, 1-1... up to 8-8).',
      equipment: 'Domino set, score sheet.',
      dealing: "2 players: 8-9 tiles each. 3 players: 7 tiles each. 4 players: 8 tiles each. Remaining tiles form the 'Stamm' (Boneyard).",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Leading**: The player with the heaviest tile (8-7 being the heaviest in this set) leads first. 2. **Matching**: On your turn, you must place a tile where one of its ends matches an available end on the board. 3. **The Draw**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you find a playable tile. (Common house rule: maximum of 3 draws). 4. **Passing**: If the boneyard is empty and you cannot play, you pass. 5. **Ending**: A round ends when one player 'Dominoes' (empties their hand) or when the game is blocked.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Austrian Dominoes is a draw-and-match game with no betting or ante.',
      deal: 'Dealing is done via custom deal_tiles action; no generic deal action.',
      reveal_market: 'No market pile; tiles are in talon (boneyard) and hands only.',
      buy_market: 'There is no market or purchase mechanic in this domino game.',
      buy_stock: 'Players draw from talon when blocked; no buy-from-stock action.',
      fold: 'Players pass only when boneyard is empty and they cannot play.',
      check: 'No betting rounds; check does not apply to Austrian Dominoes.',
      call: 'No betting; call is not used in this domino game.',
      bet: 'Scoring is by opponent pips per round; no wagering.',
      raise: 'No betting; raise does not apply to this game.',
      declare: 'No declaration phase; players match tiles to the brick layout.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands stay private until play; no reveal-hand phase.',
      award_pot: 'Points are tallied via count_opposing_pips; no pot to award.',
      play_card: 'Tile play uses custom match_tile_brick action for brick layout.',
      draw: 'Drawing from boneyard is via custom draw_from_talon action.',
      discard: 'Tiles are played to the tableau only; no discard pile in this game.',
      pass: 'Pass occurs only when blocked and boneyard empty; no explicit pass action.',
      bid: 'No bidding; heaviest tile leads; play is match-only.',
      meld: 'No melding; tiles are matched side-by-side on the brick tableau.',
      go_out: 'Round ends when a player dominoes or game is blocked; no go_out action.',
